      "content": "that's exactly the kind of framing i'm looking for. it really cuts through the noise.\n\nto take it a step further, i want to challenge the idea that these \"mass movements\" actually have any inherent direction. how can i argue that the socioeconomic grievances were essentially just raw, unguided energy that was completely useless until robespierre provided the intellectual framework to weaponize it? i want to suggest that without his specific genius, the hunger and debt wouldn't have even led to a revolution, just a series of disconnected, meaningless riots.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
